{
  "about": [
    "How bare URLs in text become links. Two implementations follow this table:",
    "the API's markdown renderer (app/utils/markdown_inline.py, tested in",
    "tests/unit/test_markdown.py) and the frontend's plain-text linkifier",
    "(<shuushuu-frontend-repo>/src/lib/utils/linkify.ts). This copy in the API",
    "repo is the original; the frontend keeps an identical copy. Change both",
    "together. Each case is one line of text with no markdown in it. A segment",
    "is either plain text (a string) or a link (href as typed, plus the text shown)."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no url",
      "text": "no links here",
      "segments": [
        "no links here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "https url",
      "text": "https://a.example/x",
      "segments": [
